{"id":"neet-2025-q149","pn":149,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Biomolecules (Biology)","st":"Enzymes, apoenzyme","q":"The protein portion of an enzyme is called:","o":["Cofactor","Coenzyme","Apoenzyme","Prosthetic group"],"c":2,"s":"In many cases non-protein parts called co-factors are bound to the enzyme to make it catalytically active.\nIn these cases the protein portion of the enzyme is called the apoenzyme.\nThree kinds of co-factors: prosthetic groups, co-enzymes and metal ions.\nProsthetic groups are organic compounds tightly bound to the apoenzyme.\nCo-enzymes are also organic compounds but their association with the apoenzyme is only transient."}
